I didn't call the coffee chain a bluff, since you don't know whether it's real. The letter treats it as possible but uncertain. I also added that your offer reaches about $5,740 by year five, which is above what he's asking.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Lease renewal – Pho Lan\n\nDear Frank,\n\nThank you for sending the renewal terms. I want to stay, and I'd like to find a number that works for both of us.\n\nI can't pay $5,650 a month and keep the restaurant open. What I can offer is $5,100 a month on a new five-year lease, with 3% increases each year after the first. That brings the rent to about $5,740 by year five.\n\nHere is why I think this is a good deal for you:\n\n- I've been your tenant for ten years, over two leases.\n- In 2019 I put about $70,000 into the kitchen, including the hood system, which stays with the building. A new restaurant would spend around $40,000 to install one.\n- Your proposed rent works out to about $29 a square foot. The unit two doors down has been listed at $28 for 14 months and is still empty.\n\nI know you've had other interest in the space. What I can offer is a tenant with a long record here and no gap in rent.\n\nAbout early 2024: our walk-in cooler failed and we were closed for nine days, which is why two payments were late. Thank you for waiving the fees. I've paid on time every month since. Under the new lease I'll pay by automatic bank transfer on the 1st of each month.\n\nIf we agree on terms, I'll sign within two weeks. Could you let me have your answer by June 1? That gives me time to plan before the current lease ends in August.\n\nThank you, Frank. I hope we can keep working together.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your name]\nPho Lan\n</final_document>","ttft_ms":10518,"type":"result","duration_ms":16196,"uuid":"06ad3086-4060-4fae-a3b6-71f602046bed","ttft_stream_ms":647,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":647,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens"